## What I did

Read the spec first (`references/hint-design.md`), surveyed the app, injected hints across all screens, then validated statically **and** at runtime.

The app is a Chinese intangible-heritage showcase (Vite + React + shadcn, 8 heritage items, 3 routes, two view modes on `/`).

**Screens & components annotated** — 10 files, 83 hinted elements:

| Screen | Components |
|---|---|
| Global chrome | `Header` (brand, 3 nav links, CTA), `Footer` (2 link lists) |
| Home `/` | `HeroSection` (CTAs + stats), `HeritageListing`, `HeritageCard` |
| Panorama `/?view=panorama` | `Index` section, `PanoramaViewer` (hotspots, zoom, loading), `HeritageOverlay` dialog |
| Detail `/heritage/:id` | `HeritageDetail` (breadcrumb, gallery, fields, actions) + its "not found" branch |
| 404 | `NotFound` |

**Id namespaces:** `nav.*`, `hero.*`, `heritage.listing/filters/results/grid.*`, `heritage.detail.*`, `heritage.overlay.*`, `panorama.*`, `footer.*`, `notfound.*`.

**Collections — all six fold**, confirmed in a live DOM: `heritage.grid` (8), `panorama.hotspots` (4), `hero.stats` (4), `footer.categories` (4), `footer.about` (4), `heritage.detail.gallery` (3). None failed to fold.

## Verification beyond the linter

The validator reported **0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 info**, but it's static-only. Since several hints sit on `framer-motion` components — which could have silently dropped `data-*` before reaching the DOM — I built an IIFE bundle and rendered all four screens in jsdom. Hints reach the DOM everywhere, **zero duplicate ids on every screen**, and no element lands in `other`. I also exercised the conditional UI: opening the overlay (78 hints on-page, no collision) and forcing empty results, which confirmed `heritage.filters.clear` and `heritage.results.empty.clear` coexist without clashing — the one real uniqueness trap in this app.

**Project checks:** `tsc` clean, `build` succeeds. `lint` shows 4 errors/7 warnings — **all pre-existing**; the only one in a file I touched (`HeritageListing`, `setSortBy(v as any)`) is present verbatim in the pristine copy. The CSS `@import` build warning is also pre-existing.

## Three code changes beyond adding attributes

1. `HeritageCard` gained a `collectionId` prop, so item ids are scoped by collection (§8) rather than hardcoded.
2. Hero stats and both footer lists were index-/label-keyed; I added stable `key` fields so item ids aren't array-index-keyed (§7 rule 2). Same rendered output.
3. `HeritageDetail` gained a pure `imageKey()` helper deriving gallery keys from image filenames — the thumbnails had no stable key but the index. I verified no collisions across all 8 items' images.

## Deliberately left unhinted

Card description paragraphs (line-clamped, 8× long Chinese text — expensive on every snapshot), the overlay's non-interactive thumbnail strip, static headings/marketing copy and the panorama instruction line, decorative gradients/patterns/scroll indicator, icon SVGs adjacent to labelled controls, and all `components/ui/*` primitives (hinted at call sites instead — no prop-widening was needed, as `Input` and `SelectTrigger` already spread props).

One limitation worth flagging: `SelectItem` options only exist in the DOM while the menu is open, and Radix's menu wouldn't open under jsdom, so their ids are validated statically only. This matters little in practice — each trigger carries `data-semtag-options` built from the same source that renders the menu, which is what lets the agent pick a value without opening it.

